[I] NVM-Express user space tooling for Linux

[T] nvme-cli is the command line utility to manage NVM Express (NVMe)
[T] storage devices on Linux. It is built on libnvme and can identify
[T] controllers and namespaces, read logs and SMART data, update firmware,
[T] format devices and connect to NVMe over Fabrics targets.

[U] https://github.com/linux-nvme/nvme-cli

[A] Nvme-cli Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/base
[F] CROSS
[R] - avr32 openrisc

[V] 2.16
[L] GPL

[CV-FLAGS] NO-MAJOR
[D] cf20000bca7375a409dbd8a96b2b710fb39e9469b73eca6f84ed558b nvme-cli-2.16.tar.gz https://github.com/linux-nvme/nvme-cli/archive/v2.16/

